# Global TrustTicker requirements

TrustTicker is an **informational market-intelligence product**. It does not execute orders.

## Do not

- Add brokerage execution
- Present personalized buy or sell instructions
- Claim or imply guaranteed profits
- Display expected profit, target prices, or probability of success
- Claim latency or reliability targets have been achieved without adequate reproducible production samples
- Cherry-pick performance or latency records
- Copy Arcane Monitor branding, artwork, source code, proprietary assets, or exact visual styling

## Security

- Never trust a client-provided `userId`
- Derive private ownership from the authenticated server session
- Scope every private query and mutation by session user
- Require server-side `requireAdmin` (or equivalent) on every admin page, API, and server action
- Keep cron authentication fail-closed
- Rate-limit sensitive and computationally expensive endpoints
- Use least-privilege Prisma selects
- Never expose secrets, provider credentials, internal hostnames, webhook URLs, or private user data
- Analytics must use event-specific allowlists

Also follow `.cursor/rules/security.mdc`.

## Accuracy

- Preserve source timestamps, sequence numbers, and data-quality states
- Never silently substitute missing values
- Distinguish unavailable, stale, estimated, and verified data
- Quarantine ambiguous ticker resolution
- Preserve calculation and rule versions
- Every calculated state must be explainable

## Product

- Separate momentum intensity, attention priority, tradeability, directional implication, and risk
- Never use an attention score as a recommendation
- Major trader-interface changes must update the Platform Guide version, copy, and `data-guide` targets (see `.cursor/rules/platform-guide.mdc`)
- Maintain keyboard and screen-reader accessibility
- Use feature flags and backward-compatible migrations
